MaterialX material graph support includes mathematical shader implementations
from Academy Software Foundation MaterialX 1.39.5 and Autodesk Aurora. Original
copyright and license notices, source versions, hashes and adaptation records
are preserved under third_party/materialx and third_party/aurora. MaterialX
noise and HSV color operators additionally retain their Sony Pictures Imageworks
/ OSL BSD notices. The native Disney, glTF, USD Preview and Chiang hair models,
and hex-tiling pattern adaptations, are recorded in third_party/materialx/ORIGIN.md.
The generated official gallery uses the pinned MaterialX v1.39.5 example assets;
its source/resource copies include the upstream license and third-party notices.
USD and MaterialX Python libraries are external asset-tool dependencies only.

Numerical reference for triangle reconstruction and projected roundoff bounds:
  Dirk Gerrit van Antwerpen, NVIDIA, 2023:
  "Solving Self-Intersection Artifacts in DirectX Raytracing"
  https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/solving-self-intersection-artifacts-in-directx-raytracing/
Caustra applies these bounds to homogeneous-medium collision positions and
surface/NEE ray endpoints. Medium collision corrections are limited to the
traversed segment; sampled distances and transport PDFs are kept separate
from this numerical placement correction.

